From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:19:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 135/159] [ae-patch] Remove a personal Claude login from
 Settings

Settings, Claude accounts could rename an extra Claude login but never remove
it: no delete existed at any layer. A new credential kind, claude-oauth-delete,
runs through the same seams as rename (the server allowlist, the host frame
handler, the account logic, the web kind union). It refuses the default CLI
login and shared accounts, drops the name, its label and its token, and falls
back to the default login when the removed account was the one new chats used.
Running chats keep the token they launched with. The full Settings view shows
Remove beside Rename on every personal login, asking once; the compact picker
and the default CLI login get no Remove.
